Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:03:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 43/69] dt-bindings: display: simple-framebuffer: Add backlight

Allow describing the backlight of the panel that shows the framebuffer,
so that the OS can turn it off while the display is blanked.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml     | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
index 45ffdebc9..dbfb71854 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
@@ -126,6 +126,12 @@ properties:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description: Display panel node
 
+  backlight:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      Backlight of the panel showing the framebuffer. The OS can turn it off
+      while the display is blanked.
+
   allwinner,pipeline:
     description: Pipeline used by the framebuffer on Allwinner SoCs
     enum:
